---
import Fastfetch from "@/components/sections/about/Fastfetch.astro";
import SkillsGrid from "@/components/sections/about/SkillsGrid.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-16 min-h-svh" aria-label="About">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4.5">
      <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight tracking-tight font-600">About</h1>
      <p class="color-portfolio-muted leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        Hi! I am Julian Peter Gerona. I'm a 4th year Information Technology
        student at Mapúa Malayan Colleges Laguna, specializing in
        cybersecurity. I build web and mobile software:
        interfaces in React and Astro, APIs in Express and Django, native
        Android in Kotlin with Jetpack Compose.
      </p>
      <p class="color-portfolio-muted leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        AI is part of how I build, and it has made me faster at turning ideas
        into working software. My software engineering background is what makes
        it work: I design the architecture, direct the tools, and make the
        final calls on what ships.
      </p>
      <p class="color-portfolio-muted leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        I try to live by kaizen, the Japanese idea of improving a little every
        day. I would rather get steadily better than wait to be perfect, so I
        keep studying, keep building, and let the small gains compound.
      </p>
    </div>

    <SkillsGrid />

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4.5">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
        <h2 class="text-[1.375rem] leading-tight font-400 font-serif">Setup</h2>
        <p class="text-sm color-portfolio-muted leading-snug max-w-prose">
          My 13-inch MacBook Air from 2015 has carried me through every
          project on this site, from first-year machine problems to my
          practicum. It's been slow for years, but it hasn't quit, and
          everything I've shipped so far has shipped from it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Fastfetch />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
